WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.563
Look at the diagram.

00:00:01.563 --> 00:00:07.189
At the top, far above Earth's orbit, is the James Webb Space Telescope .

00:00:07.189 --> 00:00:09.221
Not in orbit around Earth.

00:00:09.221 --> 00:00:14.300
Around a point in space that doesn't exist in any material sense.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:17.504
The second Sun-Earth Lagrange point — L2.

00:00:17.504 --> 00:00:22.349
Imagine a line from the Sun, through Earth, extending outward.

00:00:22.349 --> 00:00:37.822
One and a half million kilometers past Earth, in that exact direction, the combined gravity of the Sun and the Earth, plus the centripetal force of orbiting the Sun at Earth's pace, all balance out.

00:00:37.822 --> 00:00:49.153
A spacecraft placed there moves at exactly the same angular speed as Earth — completes one orbit per year — without burning fuel to hold station.

00:00:49.153 --> 00:00:51.888
But L2 is an unstable saddle point.

00:00:51.888 --> 00:00:56.264
Drift left or right, and gravity pulls you further away.

00:00:56.264 --> 00:01:04.625
So JWST doesn't sit at L2 — it orbits around L2, in a slow loop that takes about six months per revolution.

00:01:04.625 --> 00:01:05.641
A halo orbit.

00:01:05.641 --> 00:01:11.424
It never crosses the L2 point exactly; it traces a wide ellipse around it.

00:01:11.424 --> 00:01:12.987
Why L2 specifically?

00:01:12.987 --> 00:01:13.924
Two reasons.

00:01:13.924 --> 00:01:19.004
First — Earth sits between JWST and the Sun, almost continuously.

00:01:19.004 --> 00:01:30.178
The telescope's enormous sunshield, the size of a tennis court, permanently blocks sunlight and the heat radiating from the Earth and the Moon.

00:01:30.178 --> 00:01:41.353
JWST operates at forty Kelvin — about minus two hundred and thirty Celsius — because the heat-shield geometry never lets the cold side warm up.

00:01:41.353 --> 00:01:55.966
Second — by orbiting the Sun at Earth's pace, JWST stays close enough for high-bandwidth radio links, but far enough that the Earth's thermal emissions don't blind its infrared detectors.

00:01:55.966 --> 00:02:05.343
Hubble lives in low Earth orbit, five hundred fifty kilometers up, because it observes in visible and ultraviolet light.

00:02:05.343 --> 00:02:12.533
JWST lives at L2, one and a half million kilometers up, because it observes in the infrared.

00:02:12.533 --> 00:02:13.939
Different problem.

00:02:13.939 --> 00:02:15.190
Different orbit.

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:16.284
Same universe.

